            "en": "With Midjourney, many workflows favor a compact, image-first prompt: subject and visual idea early, then light, lens, and atmosphere in short clauses. Long process notes can get diluted, so keep the scene compressed and use the controls your current interface exposes. Example: “potter rinsing a wide bowl at a studio sink, clay-dusted apron, cool north window light from left, warm bulb in the back, 50mm, hands in focus, shelves of unfinished pots in shadow, quiet editorial photography --ar 3:2.” Check current parameter support rather than copying old flags.",
            "zh": "在 Midjourney 里，很多工作流偏好紧凑、以画面为先的提示词：主体和视觉想法先出现，随后用短句补充光线、镜头和氛围。过长的流程说明容易被稀释，所以要把场景压缩，并使用当前界面提供的控制。示例：“potter rinsing a wide bowl at a studio sink, clay-dusted apron, cool north window light from left, warm bulb in the back, 50mm, hands in focus, shelves of unfinished pots in shadow, quiet editorial photography --ar 3:2”。使用前确认当前版本是否支持这些参数，不要照抄旧写法。"
