            "en": "Seedream often rewards a more explicit, ordered description: full sentences, clear positions, and counts for important objects. Keep the action in the main clause. Nano Banana is usually used as a conversation: set the base scene, attach a reference if the pot or person needs to stay consistent, then ask for one change at a time — “keep the framing, make the window light cooler, remove the cloth from the foreground.” Do not assume identical controls across interfaces.",
